# Form Fields

Primitives live under `src/components/forms/base/`. Domain-specific fields live under `src/components/forms/` (and feature folders). Reuse both before inventing new inputs or label/error layout.

## Field vs FieldBase

| | `Field*` (e.g. `FieldText`) | `FieldBase*` (e.g. `FieldBaseText`) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Use when | Inside a vee-validate `useForm` / `useFormWithErrorScrolling` | Local `v-model` (modals, pickers, non-form state) |
| Binding | `name` (required). Wires `useField` + error | `v-model` + optional `error` |
| Do not | Pass `v-model` or `error` | Call `useField` inside the base |

`Field*` is a thin wrapper: `useField(name)` → `FieldBase*` with `v-model` and `:error="errorMessage"`.

Prefer `Field*` in real forms. Prefer `FieldBase*` only when there is no form context.

Some controls are vee-validate-only (`FieldImage`, `FieldFiles`, `FieldTextareaWithAttachments`): they take `name` and have no `FieldBase*` pair.

## Composed fields (outside `base/`)

Specialized fields compose a primitive instead of duplicating UI. Prefer these when they match the need:

- `FieldLanguage` — `FieldSelect` of `appLocalesArray`. Use for locale, not a hand-rolled select.
- `FieldEditableText` / `FieldBaseEditableText` — inline edit; same `Field*` vs `FieldBase*` split as the primitives.

Same rules: `FieldLanguage` / `FieldEditableText` need a form + `name`; `FieldBaseEditableText` uses `v-model`.

If you add another specialized field, put it next to these (`src/components/forms/FieldX.vue`) and wrap an existing `Field*` / `FieldBase*`. Do not copy `FieldBaseControl` markup.

## Layout: `FieldBaseControl`

Do not copy label / error / hint markup. `FieldBase*` already wraps content in `FieldBaseControl`:

Label (text, `description`, `#labelHelp`) → default slot (input) → `FieldError` → `#hint` → `#after`

- `orientation`: `"vertical"` (default) or `"horizontal"` (label left, field right from `lg:`)
- `labelClass`: replaces the default horizontal label width (`lg:w-[300px] lg:shrink-0`) so inputs share one column
- `hideLayout`: skip label/orientation chrome; still show error/hint. Use when nesting inside another `FieldBaseControl`
- Slots: `#label`, `#labelHelp`, `#hint`, `#after`. Input extras stay on the field (`#left`, `#right`, `#buttons`)

`FieldsContainer` only stacks fields (`flex-col gap-6`). It is not a field layout.

`FieldBaseCheckbox` / `FieldBaseRadio` stay inline (control + label). Do not wrap them in `FieldBaseControl`.

## Custom / composite fields

For a row that is not a single input, wrap content in `FieldBaseControl` and pass `hideLayout` to nested `Field*` so they keep their own errors without a second label column.

```vue
<FieldBaseControl
  :name="`${field.key}.kpi`"
  :label="$t(field.titleKey)"
  :required="field.required"
  orientation="horizontal"
  labelClass="tw:lg:w-[160px] tw:lg:shrink-0"
>
  <FieldAutocomplete :name="`${field.key}.kpi`" hideLayout />
  <FieldNumber :name="`${field.key}.targetValue`" hideLayout />
</FieldBaseControl>
```

Non-input content (chips, buttons) also goes in the default slot — see `TargetCustomerFormImageModalGenerate.vue`.

## New field types

- **New input primitive** (text-like, select-like): add `FieldBaseX.vue` in `base/` (wrap with `FieldBaseControl`, extend `FieldInputBasicProps`), then `FieldX.vue` with `name` + `useField` (same pattern as `FieldText.vue`).
- **Specialized wrapper** (fixed options or extra behavior on an existing input): add `src/components/forms/FieldX.vue` that renders a `Field*` / `FieldBase*` (same pattern as `FieldLanguage.vue`).
- Do not duplicate `FieldLabel` / `FieldError` / `FieldHint` / `FieldBaseControl` markup.
